cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its results, please cite the archived version below
  and the paper "Simple repair policies with delays for systems with
  simultaneous failures: exact costs and the value of knowing which components
  failed" by G. Lagos and H. Olivero.
type: dataset
title: >-
  Simple-delayed: code and results for “Simple repair policies with delays for
  systems with simultaneous failures”
authors:
  - given-names: Guido
    family-names: Lagos
    affiliation: Universidad Adolfo Ibáñez, Viña del Mar, Chile
  - given-names: Héctor
    family-names: Olivero
    affiliation: Instituto de Ingeniería Matemática, Universidad de Valparaíso, Chile
version: v1.0.0
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/guidolagos/Simple-delayed
abstract: >-
  Julia code, experiment grid, structural signatures and computed results of
  the computational study of the paper “Simple repair policies with delays for
  systems with simultaneous failures: exact costs and the value of knowing
  which components failed”. For the 20 benchmark networks of Yeh et al.
  (2024), 31 Lévy-frailty Marshall-Olkin failure models and 16 repair delays
  (9,920 configurations), the code computes the exact long-run mean costs of
  all r-out-of-n repair policies with the closed forms of the paper, the
  optimal count-based policies, and the optimal state-based policies for the 18
  networks with at most 27 components. The code is released under the MIT
  License and the data and results under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - repair policies
  - signature
  - common-cause failures
  - Lévy-frailty Marshall-Olkin
  - Markov decision process
  - Julia
